  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1020 PM CST Sat Nov 21 2026\n\nCooler weather will prevail through the rest of the forecast\nperiod, though a mid week system still brings hope for widespread\nlight to moderate rainfall across Middle Tennessee. This will \ncome from a pair of upper-level disturbances attempting to merge \nacross our region and a resultant inverted surface trough\ndeveloping across the Tennessee and Ohio Valleys. Best overall\nforcing and moisture advection will occur on Wednesday and \nensemble guidance has made a fairly big uptick in PoP as a result.\nRain amounts up to ~0.50\" are forecast. No drought buster, but a \nnice soaking rain potential at least.\n\nIt appears a fairly active pattern aloft will persist across the\nregion late week, but the next chance for rain remains outside \nthis forecast period.",
